<p>Left-leaning leaders from Europe, Latin America and Africa gathered in Barcelona for a summit framed as a defense of democracy and multilateral cooperation, as organizers warned of growing pressure from far-right and authoritarian movements. Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez hosted the meeting, with Brazilian President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva as co-chair. Other participants included Mexico&#x27;s President Claudia Sheinbaum, South Africa&#x27;s President Cyril Ramaphosa, Colombia&#x27;s President Gustavo Petro, Kosovo&#x27;s Prime Minister Albin Kurti and Uruguay&#x27;s President Yamandú Orsi. Sánchez used the gathering to argue that multilateral institutions have weakened. He pointed to the war in the Middle East, the Russia-Ukraine conflict and U.S. tariffs under President Trump as signs of strain on the international order. The meeting also underscored warmer Spain-Mexico ties during Sheinbaum&#x27;s first visit to Spain since taking office in October 2024.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/76za0E-NR9mTBqBbzANI-EZD8tfJgQW04jHU4nNTOyyYfrdHceU9OO7iBMEr9yBjJb-c4f8UZTbh87E96wxtyS9mVPdI2EIARFr3WGJJOD6G' alt='Spain’s Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez and Brazil’s President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva attend the Global Progressive Mobilisation in Barcelona, Spain, April 18.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>UN reform: Sánchez called for changes to the United Nations, saying its role had been pushed aside in the Middle East and Russia-Ukraine conflicts.</li><li>Anti-elite message: Sánchez widened his critique beyond the far right, taking aim at billionaires, housing speculators and oligarchs he said exploit democratic systems for private gain.</li></ul><blockquote>We will twist the arm of the people who think they are completely untouchable. - Pedro Sánchez</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Claudia Sheinbaum: By saying Spain and Mexico were not in a diplomatic crisis, Mexico&#x27;s president cast the visit as evidence of a pragmatic thaw after years of tension over colonial-era grievances. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1993096/leftist-leaders-gather-in-spain-to-rally-against-rise-of-far-right'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Lars Klingbeil: Germany&#x27;s vice chancellor called the meeting a needed show of solidarity and cooperation at a time of growing global division. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1993096/leftist-leaders-gather-in-spain-to-rally-against-rise-of-far-right'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1993096/leftist-leaders-gather-in-spain-to-rally-against-rise-of-far-right'>Leftist leaders gather in Spain to rally against rise of far right</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/sanchez-to-twist-the-arm-of-global-right-wing-at-anti-trump-rally-progressive-left-barcelona/'>At anti-Trump rally, Sánchez promises to ‘twist the arm’ of the global right</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.elconstitucional.es/en/national/sanchez-gathers-global-progressive-leaders-in-barcelona-against-the-rise-of-the-global-far-right_3635_102.html'>Headed by Spanish prime minister Pedro Sánchez, left-wing heads of government gather at the IV Meeting in Defense of Democracy and Progressive Global Mobilization in Barcelona. Participants included Brazil&#x27;s Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva, Colombia&#x27;s Gustavo Petro, Kosovo&#x27;s Albin Kurti, Mexico&#x27;s Claudia Sheinbaum, South Africa&#x27;s Cyril Ramaphosa, and Uruguay&#x27;s Yamandú Orsi.</a> - elconstitucional.es</li></ul>